    "text": "Let $\\mathfrak{m}$ be an infinite cardinal and $G$ be a graph with chromatic number $\\mathfrak{m}$. Let $r\\geq 1$. Must $G$ contain a subgraph of chromatic number $\\mathfrak{m}$ which does not contain any odd cycle of length $\\leq r$?",
